Problem 2.1 : For adding 5.55 \times 10^4 and 6.95 \times 10^3, first the exponent is made equal. Thus 5.55 \times 10^4 + 0.695 \times 10^4. Then these numbers can be added as follows : (5.55 + 0.695) \times 10^4 = 6.245 \times 10^4
Problem 2.2: The subtraction of two numbers can be done as shown below: 3.5 \times 10^{-2} - 5.8 \times 10^{-3} = (3.5 \times 10^{-2}) - (0.58 \times 10^{-2}) = (3.5 - 0.58) \times 10^{-2} = 2.92 \times 10^{-2}
Here the decimal has to be moved four places to the right and (-4) is the exponent in the scientific notation. Now let us perform mathematical operations on numbers expressed in scientific notation.
Problem 2.3: (5.6 \times 10^{5}) \times (6.9 \times 10^{8})
= (5.6 \times 6.9) (10^{5+8})
= (5.6 \times 6.9) \times 10^{13}
= 38.64 \times 10^{13}
= 3.864 \times 10^{14}
Problem 2.4: (9.8 \times 10^{-2}) \times (2.5 \times 10^{-6})
= (9.8 \times 2.5) (10^{-2 + (-6)})
= (9.8 \times 2.5) \times (10^{-2-6})
= 24.50 \times 10^{-8}
= 2.45 \times 10^{-7}
